2. State Space and Dynamics

2.1 State Space Definition

Let the joint configuration space be Q ⊂ ℝ^n with n = 17 active degrees of freedom (wrist 2, thumb 3, index 3, middle 3, ring 3, little 3). Let the tendon length and tension spaces be L ⊂ ℝ^m and T ⊂ ℝ^m with m = 6 tendons. The world state space is W ⊂ ℝ^{d_w}.

The contact state at a single point is defined as

c_i = (p_i, n_i, f_i) ∈ ℝ³ × S² × ℝ³,

with dim c_i = 3 + 2 + 3 = 8. The normal and tangential components of the contact force decompose as

f_i = f_{n,i} n_i + f_{t,i}, f_{t,i} ∈ T_{n_i}S² ≅ ℝ².

The friction coefficient is not a per-contact state variable. It is a property of the material pair, defined as

μ_i = μ(elastomer, μ_o), μ_o ∈ ℝ_+,

where μ_o belongs to the world state w. For k simultaneous contact points, the contact manifold has dimension

dim C = 8k.

The complete state is

x = (q, q̇, L, τ, c, w) ∈ X,

with

dim X = 2n + 2m + 8k + d_w = 46 + 8k + d_w.

Under the quasi-static assumption introduced below, the velocity subspace TQ is removed from the state for instantaneous analysis, giving

dim X_qs = n + 2m + 8k + d_w = 29 + 8k + d_w.

Scope assumption. The world state w includes a single material-pair friction coefficient μ_o. This restricts the analysis to objects with homogeneous surface material. Multi-material objects would require per-region friction parameters, which is left for future work.

2.2 Dynamics with Underactuation and Contact Coupling

The full rigid-body dynamics with contact are

M(q)q̈ + C(q, q̇)q̇ + g(q) = B(q)τ + B_wrist u_wrist − Σ_{i=1}^k J_i(q)^T f_i,

where M(q) ∈ ℝ^{n×n} is the joint-space inertia matrix, C(q, q̇) ∈ ℝ^{n×n} captures Coriolis and centrifugal effects, g(q) ∈ ℝ^n is the gravity vector, B(q) ∈ ℝ^{n×m} is the tendon-to-joint transmission matrix, B_wrist ∈ ℝ^{n×2} is the direct-drive wrist actuation matrix, and J_i(q) ∈ ℝ^{3×n} is the point-contact Jacobian. The contact force f_i ∈ ℝ³ enters the dynamics explicitly, and J_i^T f_i ∈ ℝ^n is dimensionally consistent.

Underactuation. The total actuation map is

B_total(q) = [B(q) B_wrist] ∈ ℝ^{n×(m+2)} = ℝ^{17×8}.

The actuation-unreachable subspace is the orthogonal complement of the image of B_total:

U(q) = (Im B_total(q))^⊥ = ker B_total(q)^T ⊂ ℝ^n.

Its dimension is

dim U(q) = n − rank(B_total(q)).

For generic configurations where B_total has full column rank 8,

dim U(q) = 17 − 8 = 9.

These 9 directions are not directly actuated by tendon tension or wrist motors. The term "null space" is reserved for ker B_total(q) ⊂ ℝ^{m+2}, which is generically {0} when B_total has full column rank.

Assumption 2.1 (Quasi-static equilibrium with compliance). Under quasi-static conditions q̈ ≈ 0, q̇ ≈ 0, the system satisfies

g(q) + Σ_{i=1}^k J_i(q)^T f_i ∈ Im B_total(q) + K(q),

where K(q) ⊂ ℝ^n is the compliance-induced wrench subspace generated by elastic joint and tendon deflections. The subspace K(q) is defined explicitly as

K(q) = { K_q Δq + B(q) K_t ΔL : Δq ∈ ℝ^n, ΔL ∈ ℝ^m },

where K_q ∈ ℝ^{n×n} is the joint stiffness matrix and K_t ∈ ℝ^{m×m} is the tendon stiffness matrix. The equilibrium manifold is

E = { (q, τ, c) ∈ Q × T × C : g(q) + Σ_{i=1}^k J_i(q)^T f_i − B_total(q) [τ; u_wrist] ∈ K(q) }.

The equilibrium condition is an inclusion, not an equality. The compliance subspace K(q) resolves the underactuation by allowing the actuation-unreachable directions to be determined by elastic deflections rather than by tendon tension.

Tendon dynamics. The tendon lengths evolve according to

L_{t+1} = L_t + ΔL(τ_t, q_t) + w_t^L,

where ΔL captures configuration-dependent elongation and Bowden-cable hysteresis. The tendon tensions evolve according to

τ_{t+1} = τ_t + Δτ(u_t, τ_t, q_t) + w_t^τ.

2.3 Joint Error from Tendon Compliance

The configuration-dependent joint error is

q_actual = q_commanded + Δq_compliance(τ, q) + η_compliance,

where the compliance-weighted pseudoinverse is defined as

Δq_compliance = (K_q + B K_t B^T)^{-1} B K_t ΔL,

and η_compliance captures the component in the actuation-unreachable subspace U(q). The minimum-norm pseudoinverse B^† corresponds to the limit K_q → 0, which is not physical. The compliance-weighted form is the correct equilibrium map.

