4. Probabilistic Graphical Model

4.1 Wrist State as Separator

The wrist force/torque measurement z_W is a common child of the hand-side state X_A and the forearm-side state X_B. Conditioning on a common child couples its parents. The correct graphical structure introduces the wrist pose x_wrist ∈ SE(3) as an explicit separator variable:

X_A ⫫ X_B | x_wrist.

Equivalently,

p(X_A | X_B, x_wrist) = p(X_A | x_wrist).

The F/T measurement satisfies

z_W = h_W(X_A, X_B) + v_W,

and is a coupling factor, not a separator.

4.2 Information Matrix Structure

The information matrix has the block structure

Λ = [ Λ_A Λ_{A,B} Λ_{A,W} ;
Λ_{A,B}^T Λ_B Λ_{B,W} ;
Λ_{A,W}^T Λ_{B,W}^T Λ_W ],

where Λ_{A,B} ≠ 0 arises from the F/T factor. Marginalizing the wrist state yields the Schur complement

Λ_A' = Λ_A − [Λ_{A,B} Λ_{A,W}] [Λ_B Λ_{B,W}; Λ_{B,W}^T Λ_W]^{-1} [Λ_{A,B}^T; Λ_{A,W}^T].

The coupling term Λ_{A,B} cannot be neglected: the F/T factor directly connects hand and forearm variables.

4.3 Factor Graph and MAP Estimation

The joint distribution factorizes as

p(V | Z) ∝ Π_{f_i ∈ F} f_i(V_i),

with Gaussian factors

f_i(V_i) ∝ exp(−½ ‖h_i(V_i) − z_i‖²_{R_i^{-1}}).

The MAP estimate is the nonlinear least-squares solution

V̂ = argmin_V Σ_{f_i ∈ F} ‖r_i(V_i)‖²_{R_i^{-1}},

solved by Gauss–Newton iteration.

