5. Observability Theory

5.1 Discrete-Time Observability

Consider the nonlinear discrete-time system

x_{t+1} = f(x_t, u_t) + w_t, z_t = h(x_t) + v_t.

The local observability matrix over a window of length L is

O(x_{t−L:t}) = [ H_t ; H_{t−1} F_{t−1} ; … ; H_{t−L} Π_{k=0}^{L−1} F_{t−1−k} ],

where H_s = ∂h/∂x|{x_s} and F_s = ∂f/∂x|{x_s}.

5.2 Assumptions

Assumption 5.1 (Quasi-static manipulation). The system operates in the quasi-static regime with q̈ ≈ 0, q̇ ≈ 0. The equilibrium condition is the inclusion of Assumption 2.1.

Assumption 5.2 (Occlusion). The external camera is occluded by the hand: M_vis(q, w) = 0, and

∂h_{vis, ext}/∂(c, w) = 0.

Assumption 5.3 (Tactile rank). The tactile Jacobian ∂z_T/∂c has rank 8k on an open set where G_object is known and shear is detectable.

Assumption 5.4 (Transversality). For k ≥ 2, the contact positions {p_i} are pairwise distinct and non-collinear, and the contact forces satisfy f_i ≠ 0. Under these conditions, the F/T Jacobian H_FT ∈ ℝ^{6×8k} has full row rank 6, and its row space is contained in the row space of the tactile Jacobian H_T ∈ ℝ^{8k×8k}. The intersection dimension is exactly 6.

Assumption 5.5 (Internal perception rank). The internal camera Jacobian J_Φ J_Ψ has rank m_int ≤ 3 for the bundle-view geometry with retro-reflective markers on tendon terminations, with markers staggered in depth by at least 5 mm.

Assumption 5.6 (Persistent excitation). Over the window, the contact configuration evolves such that

rank [ H_t^T, F_{t−1}^T H_{t−1}^T, …, Π F^T H_{t−L}^T ]^T = dim X_qs.

5.3 Instantaneous Rank Analysis

Lemma 5.1 (External architecture under occlusion). Under Assumptions 5.1–5.2 and quasi-static reduction on X_qs, the rank of the external architecture measurement Jacobian satisfies

rank(H_ext) ≤ n + 6 = 23.

The instantaneous unobservable subspace has dimension at least

dim X_qs − (n + 6) = (29 + 8k + d_w) − 23 = 6 + 8k + d_w.

Proof. The external architecture has h_ext = (h_prop, h_FT, h_vis, ext). Under occlusion, h_vis, ext contributes zero rank by Assumption 5.2. Proprioception contributes n rows under quasi-static reduction on X_qs. The F/T sensor contributes at most 6 rows. The unobservable dimension follows. ∎

Lemma 5.2 (Tactile rank increase). Under Assumptions 5.3–5.4, the tactile measurement adds at least

8k − 6

independent rows beyond those contributed by proprioception and F/T. Generically, this bound is tight.

Proof. The tactile Jacobian has rank 8k by Assumption 5.3. The F/T Jacobian has rank 6 by Assumption 5.4. The row space of H_FT is contained in the row space of H_T, with intersection dimension exactly 6. Therefore the number of independent rows contributed by tactile beyond F/T is exactly 8k − 6. ∎

Lemma 5.3 (Internal perception rank increase). Under Assumption 5.5, the internal camera adds at least m_int independent rows beyond proprioception, F/T, and tactile.

Proposition 5.4 (Instantaneous rank increase under occlusion). Under Assumptions 5.1–5.5, at a state x with M_vis = 0 and k ≥ 2 contacts,

rank(H_dist) − rank(H_ext) ≥ (8k − 6) + m_int.

For k = 2 and m_int = 3, the lower bound is 16 − 6 + 3 = 13.

Proof. By Lemma 5.1, rank(H_ext) ≤ n + 6. By Lemmas 5.2 and 5.3, the distributed architecture adds at least (8k − 6) + m_int independent rows. ∎

5.4 Windowed Observability

Proposition 5.5 (Windowed rank increase). Under Assumptions 5.1–5.6, there exists an open set X_occ ⊂ X_qs such that for all x ∈ X_occ,

rank(O_dist(x)) > rank(O_ext(x)).

Proof. By Proposition 5.4, the instantaneous rank increase is at least (8k − 6) + m_int. Under Assumption 5.6, the null space of H_t is not invariant under the dynamics, so the propagated rows preserve this rank increase over the window. ∎

Corollary 5.6 (Lower bound). The windowed rank increase satisfies

rank(O_dist) − rank(O_ext) ≥ 8k − 6 + m_int.

For k ≥ 2 and m_int = 3, this is at least 13.

Remark 5.7. This is a strict rank-increase result, not a full-rank result. The architectural argument requires only strict increase. The full-rank result rank(O_dist) = dim X_qs is unverifiable without specifying d_w.

