9.4 Bus Architecture with GMSL2 Aggregation

The Orin Nano supports up to 4 CSI cameras over 8 MIPI CSI-2 lanes with a total D-PHY bandwidth of 20 Gbps. It cannot directly attach 8 cameras at 1 Mpix, 30 Hz, 12-bit raw. The bandwidth requirement is

8 × 1 × 10⁶ × 30 × 12 = 2.88 Gbps,

plus overhead ≈ 3.5 Gbps. This fits within the 20 Gbps budget.

Two MAX96724 quad deserializers aggregate 8 cameras over GMSL2 coax into MIPI CSI-2. The MAX96724 converts four GMSL2 inputs to 2× 4-lane MIPI D-PHY outputs at 2.5 Gbps per lane. The Orin Nano receives:

· 4 cameras from deserializer 1 via 4 MIPI lanes.
· 4 cameras from deserializer 2 via 4 MIPI lanes.

The forearm internal camera connects via a separate MIPI port on a companion board or is multiplexed.

Finger cameras operate at 30 Hz with 1 Mpix binning. The total MIPI load is within the 20 Gbps budget.

