11. Experimental Predictions and Falsifiability

11.1 Theoretical Predictions

1. Rank increase. Under occlusion, rank(O_dist) − rank(O_ext) ≥ 8k − 6 + m_int for generic {p_i}.
2. Information gain. ΔI_occ = I(w_local; S_dist | M=0) − I(w_local; S_ext | M=0) > 0.
3. Ablation ranking. Removing tactile sensing produces the largest rank deficiency (8k − 6 = 10 for k = 2). Removing internal perception produces the largest deficiency in the actuation-unreachable subspace (m_int = 3).

11.2 Falsifiability

The theory is falsified if:

1. rank(O_dist) − rank(O_ext) = 0 under occlusion;
2. ΔI_occ ≤ 0;
3. the ablation removing tactile sensing produces no significant drop in task success at the p < 0.05 level.

11.3 Power Analysis

For detecting a 20% reduction in occlusion-conditioned localization error with σ = 0.5 Ē, power 1 − β = 0.8, and α = 0.05,

n_trials = 2(z_{1−α/2} + z_{1−β})² σ² / Δ² ≈ 98.

We therefore require n_trials ≥ 100 per condition.

